	(text "H1–H4: shell (M3, from below) · H5–H8: Pi 5 standoffs (M2.5) · H9–H10: head brackets (M3) · FID1–3: fiducials"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 235.72 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "39808917-f0ad-5e54-8ef9-e3f66f526f36")
	)
	(text "DESIGN NOTES\n1. Inputs: USB-C 5 V (VAC1) and 12 V charging dock (VAC2) → BQ25798 buck-boost charger, NVDC power path → VSYS.\n2. VSYS (6.0–8.4 V) feeds the TB6612 directly, the always-on 3.3 V buck and the 5.15 V / 5 A Pi buck.\n3. The power switch acts on the buck enables: charging still works with the robot switched off.\n4. The ESP32 switches the Pi rail (PI_PWR_OFF) after the shutdown handshake (sheet 7).\n5. Head board (nova-head): ST7789 display, VL53L1X ToF, AT42QT1010 touch, Camera Module 3 mount.\n6. References per sheet: 2xx inputs/charger, 3xx battery/regulators, 4xx MCU, 5xx motors, 6xx sensors, 7xx Pi."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 149.86 207.78 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "02257b35-d86f-5610-aec2-06ec7f70446e")
	)
	(text "REVISIONS\nA  2026-10-24  ESP32-only robot (first release)\nB  2026-10-28  Raspberry Pi 5 edition: BQ25798 dual-input charger (USB-C + 12 V dock), 5 V / 5 A Pi rail,\n                    Pi link, VL53L4CD cliff sensors, servo; audio moved to the XVF3800 mic array"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 149.86 240.8 0)
		(effects
